    write(O/'COMPLETION_LEVELS.json',status)
    names={'anchor':'Anchor','cmi':'CMI','affine':'Affine','gp':'GP','residual':'Residual','binary':'Binary','full':'Full','mlp_adapt':'Adapted MLP','cnp':'CNP','attentioncap_adapted':'Adapted AttentionCap'}
    lines=['# Measured runtime–accuracy results','','These are completed measurements, with the exact populations and boundaries in [REPRODUCE.md](REPRODUCE.md). The main paper is six content pages plus one reference page; the expanded treatment retains the complete timing discussion and native-agreement plot.','','## Same 71 physical templates','','One CPU thread; three learned members; all 153 support samples per context. The canonical Q limit is 32, with six actual batches (mean 11.83 queries/batch). Fit costs span all six contexts and are charged once. The first optimizer initialization is included.','','| Method | NRMSE | Warm ms/Q | Q=1 mean ms | Q=1 P95 ms | Fit s | P95/P99 absolute (pF/m) |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
    for m,name in names.items():
        r=next(r for r in rows if r['task']=='fem' and r['method']==m and r['batch_limit']=='32');s=next(r for r in rows if r['task']=='fem' and r['method']==m and r['batch_limit']=='1')
        lines.append(f"| {name} | {float(r['macro_nrmse']):.5f} | {float(r['amortized_wall_ms']):.3f} | {float(s['batch_mean_ms']):.3f} | {float(s['single_request_p95_ms']):.3f} | {float(r['fit_once_all_contexts_wall_s']):.2f} | {float(r['p95_nonzero_component_absolute'])*1e12:.3f} / {float(r['p99_nonzero_component_absolute'])*1e12:.3f} |")
    lines += ['','P95/P99 pool the two nonzero physical components; component-specific values and every batch protocol are in the CSVs. No native absolute error is pooled across process-specific rule units. Anchor/CMI are more accurate than Full on this full-support cohort. Cached MLP is faster after fitting, with higher error than Anchor. The adapted AttentionCap speed is accompanied by its poor accuracy; this is not a reproduction or ranking of its original matrix-supervised task.','']
    sol=read(O/'solver_task_match.json');kernel=read(O/'native_kernel_summary.json')
    lines += ['## Matched reference and native computation','',f"Resident one-RHS fine solving averages {sol['resident_mean_total_wall_s']/71:.3f} s/geometry over three complete passes. The maximum scaled target-column versus certified-row difference is {sol['max_column_scaled_error']:.3g}. Recorded cold fine-only and certification worker-wall sums are {sol['cold_fine_wall_s']:.2f} and {sol['cold_certification_wall_s']:.2f} s, respectively. These are different timing boundaries, not interchangeable production baselines. Surrogate errors exceed reference uncertainty.",'',f"The cache-hot, resolved-width/context C++ getter counterpart averages {kernel['mean_ns']:.3f} ns/query in long loops; the ctypes loop averages {kernel['ctypes_mean_ns']/1000:.3f} microseconds/query. All 480 returned vectors are native-validated, and their supplied support knots/values match exactly. Neither number is a measured full-PEX query latency or a single-request P95.",'','## Fixed-node native deployment','','B=8, seed 11; three repetitions on each of eight unchanged layouts. The following ratios compare mean extraction wall time; fidelity uses the same original-rule reference.','','| Case | CMI ratio | Binary ratio | Full ratio | Full net-C NRMSE | Full worst-slack delta (ps) |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
    flow=list(csv.DictReader((O/'native_flow_summary.csv').open()))
    for case in sorted(set(r['case'] for r in flow)):
        sub={r['method']:r for r in flow if r['case']==case};full=sub['full']
        lines.append(f"| {case} | {float(sub['cmi']['extraction_ratio']):.3f} | {float(sub['binary']['extraction_ratio']):.3f} | {float(full['extraction_ratio']):.3f} | {json.loads(full['capacitance_metrics'])['nrmse']:.5f} | {float(full['slack_delta_ps']):+.6f} |")
    deployment=read(O/'deployment_cost.json');lines += ['',f"Shared input, model-bundle and support preparation costs {deployment['shared_comparison_setup_once_s']:.3f} s once in this comparison pipeline. The measured reuse is two designs per process, eight total. Predict/export and marginal totals are in deployment_cost.json. All electrical SPEF sections match the frozen corresponding variants. Rule registration only stores a filename; parse time remains inside extraction. Rule-only allocation and isolated parse latency are not claimed.",'','## Cost and completion levels','',f"Main measured execution: {measured:.4f} CPU core-hours. With a conservative {allowance:.2f} core-hour auxiliary allowance, budget charge is {measured+allowance:.4f}, below the 8 core-hour scope. No GPU or source training was run. Supplied characterization and selected source-stage receipts are separately listed in supplied_input_costs.json; they are not zero-cost lifecycle claims.",'']
    lines += [f'- **{k}**: {v}.' for k,v in status.items()]
    (R/'docs/runtime_accuracy_20261115/RESULTS.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
    print('resource budget charge',measured+allowance,'core-hours')
